WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.170 --> 00:00:01.859
Hey, Thoughty2 here.

00:00:01.859 --> 00:00:07.640
In Athens in the state of Georgia there is
a tree that owns itself.

00:00:07.640 --> 00:00:13.580
This tree is the only tree in the world that
is the legal landowner of the land it lives

00:00:13.580 --> 00:00:14.730
upon.

00:00:14.730 --> 00:00:19.500
Having fond memories of the tree when growing
up the landowner William H. Jackson wanted

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:21.120
to protect the tree forever.

00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:27.070
So, in the early 1800s he went to court and
transferred the deeds for the land in an eight

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:32.850
foot radius around the tree, from himself
to the tree.

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:37.969
To this day the legality of the tree's property
rights have never been questioned.

00:00:37.969 --> 00:00:45.649
Planet Earth has 57 million square miles of
land or 36 billion acres and until the day

00:00:45.649 --> 00:00:50.069
comes when we set foot on other planets that's
all the land we have.

00:00:50.069 --> 00:00:56.879
Land therefore is the most limited commodity
we have, thus it comes at a great price.

00:00:56.879 --> 00:01:02.979
As the population increases and more homes
are needed to house the next generation, the

00:01:02.979 --> 00:01:05.449
demand for land increases.

00:01:05.449 --> 00:01:09.920
In the past 10 years alone land prices have
trebled, in some countries.

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:12.700
But who owns the world?

00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:19.140
And I'm not talking about power and money
but the actual Earth you stand upon, from

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:24.679
the wilds of Alaska to Outer Mongolia who
really owns the dirt and gravel beneath your

00:01:24.679 --> 00:01:30.289
feet and more importantly who owns your house
and the land it sits on.

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:37.759
Is it really you or is it in fact the bank,
the government or some kind of land and gentry?

00:01:37.759 --> 00:01:43.560
Let's start with America and its 2.3 billion
acres of land across 50 states.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:48.729
The biggest land owner in America is cable
billionaire John Malone who owns a staggering

00:01:48.729 --> 00:01:50.850
2.2 million acres.

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:55.369
He owns enormous ranches in Wyoming, New Mexico
and Colorado.

00:01:55.369 --> 00:02:00.530
Oh, he also owns Humewood Castle in Ireland,
because he thought it was pretty.

00:02:00.530 --> 00:02:06.920
Malone is closely followed by Ted Turner who
owns 2 million acres of American land across

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.789
seven states.

00:02:08.789 --> 00:02:11.780
He is a media mogul who founded CNN.

00:02:11.780 --> 00:02:18.680
Turner's land includes 14 ranches, 28 homes
and the world's largest herd of privately

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:20.010
owned bison.

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:26.060
He also has four girlfriends, he spends a
week with each one per month, because if you're

00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:32.510
a 78-year-old billionaire who owns a massive
chunk of America then why the hell not?

00:02:32.510 --> 00:02:39.629
An Englishman's home is his castle, no matter
how big or small, your humble abode is yours

00:02:39.629 --> 00:02:42.849
and no one can ever take it away from you.

00:02:42.849 --> 00:02:44.770
Or can they?

00:02:44.770 --> 00:02:48.080
And come to think of it, is it really yours?

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:53.360
If you own your home via leasehold you have
zero rights to the ownership of your property

00:02:53.360 --> 00:02:56.760
or its land, absolutely none.

00:02:56.760 --> 00:03:01.400
You are simply renting the property and have
decided to pay for the next 99 year's rent

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.829
upfront.

00:03:02.829 --> 00:03:08.500
The freeholder is the true owner of the land
and everything upon it, he or she is your

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:12.409
landlord, for the next 99+ years.

00:03:12.409 --> 00:03:18.310
If you are wealthy enough to own a flat or
even a house in London then you probably don't

00:03:18.310 --> 00:03:21.140
actually own it, or the land.

00:03:21.140 --> 00:03:28.620
This guy does instead, 26-year-old Hugh Grovesnor,
the 7th Duke of Westminster, who owns about

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:30.150
half of London.

00:03:30.150 --> 00:03:37.540
He is worth over £12 billion, making him
the richest person under 30 years old in the

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:39.000
World.

00:03:39.000 --> 00:03:42.650
And you are simply renting from him for a
very long time.

00:03:42.650 --> 00:03:45.379
But what if you do own the freehold to your
property?

00:03:45.379 --> 00:03:50.360
And what if you've paid off your mortgage,
with no interference from the bank, you must

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:54.599
then be the one true owner of your castle
and its land?

00:03:54.599 --> 00:03:56.569
Well, not quite.

00:03:56.569 --> 00:04:01.920
I'm sorry to burst your dream of setting up
your own country in your back garden but you

00:04:01.920 --> 00:04:04.549
don't truly own any land.

00:04:04.549 --> 00:04:07.790
In fact not many people do.

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:14.439
There's a centuries old doctrine of law called
"Absolute land ownership" which is fuzzy but

00:04:14.439 --> 00:04:20.670
it means that you may hold the rights to a
piece of land and its title but you don't

00:04:20.670 --> 00:04:23.470
"absolutely" own it.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:28.750
In most countries the government owns the
entirety of the land in that country, all

00:04:28.750 --> 00:04:34.760
you own is a title to that land, giving you
certain rights to it, but not absolute ownership.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:43.130
And the government can forcefully buy your
house and land off you at any time if for

00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:48.920
example, they wish to build a bypass through
your home, well you've got to build bypasses.

00:04:48.920 --> 00:04:55.180
This is true for every country in the world,
after all if the government didn't own 100%

00:04:55.180 --> 00:05:02.100
of the land within that country then it wouldn't
be a complete country, it would be Spain,

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:06.300
minus all these plots of land where people
have purchased property.

00:05:06.300 --> 00:05:10.971
Each property owner would essentially own
their own little country and maps of the world

00:05:10.971 --> 00:05:13.770
would get really complicated.

00:05:13.770 --> 00:05:20.350
So countries have to own 100% of their land
in order to create and enforce laws within

00:05:20.350 --> 00:05:21.760
that country's boundaries.

00:05:21.760 --> 00:05:28.640
But in truth there is no such thing as true
land ownership, the laws surrounding land

00:05:28.640 --> 00:05:33.920
ownership are really messy, and change completely
depending on which country you're in.

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:39.640
In reality you have essentially paid for some
rights over a piece of land, but your rights

00:05:39.640 --> 00:05:44.710
to the land are overlapped by the rights of
other bodies, such as the government and the

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.960
monarchy, if there is one.

00:05:46.960 --> 00:05:51.240
Speaking of Monarchies, that's when things
get really complicated.

00:05:51.240 --> 00:05:57.390
For example, in England, the absolute land
owner is not the government, but The Crown,

00:05:57.390 --> 00:06:00.420
an independent body who acts on behalf of
Her Majesty the Queen.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:06.970
Queen Elizabeth II owns every square inch
of land of the United Kingdom.

00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:12.820
When you buy a property in the UK you are
simply put on a map called the "Land Registry"

00:06:12.820 --> 00:06:17.150
to identify that you own the title to that
plot of land.

00:06:17.150 --> 00:06:23.760
In reality you don't own the land, you hold
it; you are a tenant of The Crown.

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:28.620
If you were to really buy that land outright,
you would have to draw up a sales contract

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:35.990
with Her Majesty and The Government who have
certain historic legal ties with The Crown.

00:06:35.990 --> 00:06:40.320
But that would just but one less place for
Elizabeth to drive her Land Rover and walk

00:06:40.320 --> 00:06:44.630
her Corgis, so I don't think that's going
to happen.

00:06:44.630 --> 00:06:49.980
One element of the law that exemplifies the
fact that you don't actually own your own

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:57.420
land is that if you strike oil on your private
land in the UK, you have no rights to it.

00:06:57.420 --> 00:07:04.060
The Crown automatically owns any oil or other
valuable minerals found below private properties,

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:10.070
and all you're entitled to, is compensation
to replace the soil once all the oil has been

00:07:10.070 --> 00:07:15.910
extracted and sold for lots and lots of money,
none of which you will ever see.

00:07:15.910 --> 00:07:22.060
But the British isles is not all that the
Her Majesty the Queen owns, far from it.

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:28.000
As a matter of fact, Queen Elizabeth II is
the largest land owner in the world, by a

00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:30.010
large margin.

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:34.850
The Queen owns one-sixth of the Earth's land.

00:07:34.850 --> 00:07:39.520
And she is the only person in the world that
owns entire countries.

00:07:39.520 --> 00:07:46.600
Queen Elizabeth II owns 6.6 billion acres
of land and she is head of state of 16 countries,

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:49.320
collectively known as the Commonwealth Realm.

00:07:49.320 --> 00:07:54.450
She owns the entire countries of Canada and
Australia, which are the second and sixth

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:57.740
largest countries in the world, respectively.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:08:03.740
The Queen's total landholdings are worth an
estimated £25 trillion.

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:10.470
Which makes her, by a considerable margin,
the wealthiest person on the planet.

00:08:10.470 --> 00:08:16.280
But it's not quite as simple as that, she
is more of a ceremonial owner of said countries.

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:21.790
Whilst she does technically own the land,
the individual country's governments have

00:08:21.790 --> 00:08:26.050
ownership to the titles of the lands and they
profit from it.

00:08:26.050 --> 00:08:30.720
The Crown doesn't actually see any profit
from much of its land holdings.

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:37.620
Because of this the Queen's actual estimated
wealth is somewhere around £275 million.

00:08:37.620 --> 00:08:43.620
I mean that's not to be sniffed at, but it's
rather measly for someone who owns one-sixth

00:08:43.620 --> 00:08:46.110
of the planet, excluding oceans.

00:08:46.110 --> 00:08:52.579
She also owns a drive-thru McDonald's in Slough,
because why not when you're the Queen.

00:08:52.579 --> 00:08:58.519
But symbolic or not she is undoubtedly the
world's largest landholder.

00:08:58.519 --> 00:09:01.510
So who then, is following in her footsteps?

00:09:01.510 --> 00:09:07.490
That would be King Salman of Saudi Arabia,
who inherited The Kingdom of Saudi Arabia

00:09:07.490 --> 00:09:11.000
after the recent death of his half-brother
King Abdullah.

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:19.240
He owns 553 million acres in total, just 8%
of what the Queen owns.

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:26.550
But those 553 million acres are rich in oil,
which gives The Kingdom of Saudi Arabia a

00:09:26.550 --> 00:09:29.589
GDP of $646 billion.

00:09:29.589 --> 00:09:33.890
At number three on the land owner list is
none other than Pope Francis.

00:09:33.890 --> 00:09:38.839
The pope owns the Vatican City, which is its
own nation state.

00:09:38.839 --> 00:09:43.990
But isn't the Vatican also the smallest country
in the World?

00:09:43.990 --> 00:09:50.089
Yes, it most definitely is, at just 108 acres.

00:09:50.089 --> 00:09:54.180
So how does that make the Pope the world's
third largest landowner?

00:09:54.180 --> 00:10:04.019
Well, the Catholic church actually owns 177
million acres of land world-wide, which means

00:10:04.019 --> 00:10:07.769
the Pope owns 177 million acres of land.

00:10:07.769 --> 00:10:14.139
That of course includes every religious institution,
diocese and Vatican-owned embassies to the

00:10:14.139 --> 00:10:18.310
Holy See, which are in 81 countries.

00:10:18.310 --> 00:10:24.990
If all land was divided equally between every
person on the planet then every single person

00:10:24.990 --> 00:10:28.910
would own roughly 5 acres of land.

00:10:28.910 --> 00:10:31.749
Just over 3 football pitches each.

00:10:31.749 --> 00:10:38.889
But of course it isn't, land ownership has
always been about power, wealth and social

00:10:38.889 --> 00:10:41.230
class and it still is.

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:45.880
Every time you mow your lawn you are imitating
the aristocrats of the past.

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:51.550
In a figurative sense, because of course,
wealthy aristocrats definitely didn't mow

00:10:51.550 --> 00:10:53.019
their own lawns.

00:10:53.019 --> 00:10:58.570
You see the reason lawns were invented in
the first place was to show off and demonstrate

00:10:58.570 --> 00:10:59.839
power.

00:10:59.839 --> 00:11:04.800
It was a way of saying, hey look everyone,
we're so bloody rich we can afford to own

00:11:04.800 --> 00:11:08.819
and maintain vast areas of land which we have
no real use for.

00:11:08.819 --> 00:11:14.300
But look, isn't it impressive, with its shrubberies,
mazes and fountains.

00:11:14.300 --> 00:11:17.069
Yes, lots and lots of fountains.

00:11:17.069 --> 00:11:24.110
In medieval times 100% of the land your average
person owned was used to either build upon

00:11:24.110 --> 00:11:28.199
and live in, or to grow food to feed your
family.

00:11:28.199 --> 00:11:32.480
Most people would starve if they decided to
grow topiary instead of cabbages.

00:11:32.480 --> 00:11:35.990
You can't eat topiary, I've tried.

00:11:35.990 --> 00:11:42.060
So wealthy kings, princes, lords and ladies
would purposely clear all trees from their

00:11:42.060 --> 00:11:49.290
excessive areas of unused land and grow grass
upon it instead, creating a meadow or lawn.

00:11:49.290 --> 00:11:51.560
This served two purposes.

00:11:51.560 --> 00:11:56.220
Firstly it was now far easier to see people
trying to invade their castle and secondly

00:11:56.220 --> 00:12:00.710
they could show off how much spare land they
had.

00:12:00.710 --> 00:12:06.689
This was even more impressive back then because
of course, the lawn mower didn't exist.

00:12:06.689 --> 00:12:12.980
Neatly trimmed grass lawns has to be painstakingly
cut by hand by servants wielding scythes and

00:12:12.980 --> 00:12:14.339
shears.

00:12:14.339 --> 00:12:18.970
The Palace of Versailles is a prime example
of this showy-offery.

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:23.949
Even with modern gardening tools, the amount
of money, time and manpower that goes into

00:12:23.949 --> 00:12:29.550
maintaining a garden this stunning is rather
impressive.

00:12:29.550 --> 00:12:34.389
The trend of maintaining lawns to impress
others has continued throughout the centuries.

00:12:34.389 --> 00:12:39.650
And although the lawns have become significantly
smaller with an increasing population, your

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:44.731
neighbour will probably still sneer at it,
if you don't keep it nicely trimmed, because

00:12:44.731 --> 00:12:48.649
this medieval tradition has become ingrained
within our culture.

00:12:48.649 --> 00:12:55.189
But who cares if its exorbitant and a completely
unnecessary, you are the king of your castle.

00:12:55.189 --> 00:13:02.170
And okay you don't really own it, but who
